This file contains more detailed doctests for the stdnum.eu.eori module.

>>> from stdnum.eu import eori
>>> from stdnum.exceptions import *

EORI numbers are normalised and have a two-letter country code followed by at
most 15 alphanumeric characters.

>>> eori.compact('es- b64717838')
'ESB64717838'
>>> eori.validate('ESB64717838')
'ESB64717838'

Invalid lengths and characters are rejected.

>>> eori.validate('ES')
Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
InvalidLength: ...
>>> eori.validate('DE1234567890123456')
Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
InvalidLength: ...
>>> eori.validate('E112345678')
Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
InvalidFormat: ...
>>> eori.is_valid('ES123/456')
False
